{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>You shook the earth</b> — Israel, when they heard that David was weakened, like an earthquake." "<b>You shattered</b> — it has no [cognate with] evil, and its meaning is like its [parallel in] מקומו, and the heh is weak [i.e., quiescent] in place of alef, for the letters alef, heh, vav, yod interchange." "<b>For the staff</b> — at the falling [?] of mountains."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:20.520128364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}